# AFW runtime model

Permanent mental model for `libafw` script/value work. Deeper detail: `afw-value-memory`, `afw-script-eval`, `afw-compiler-ebnf`, `@AGENTS.md`.

## Core idea
- **Metadata-driven C runtime** + Python **afwdev**; interfaces and Adaptive Script share the same **immutable value graph**.
- Every significant entity is `afw_value_t` (`inf` + payload). Evaluate with `afw_value_evaluate` / `inf->optional_evaluate` (lazy; missing evaluate ⇒ value as-is).

## Value graph (non-dataType nodes)
Important infs: `compiled_value`, `block`, `call`, `call_built_in_function`, `call_script_function`, `script_function_definition`, `closure_binding`, `list_expression`, `object_expression`, `qualified_variable_reference`, `reference_by_key`, `symbol_reference`, `assignment_target`, `template_definition` (plus data-type values).

- **`compiled_value`**: self-contained unit with its own pool (`full_source`, literals, `top_block`, `root_value`, …). Releasing it destroys that pool unless survivors are referenced/reparented.
- **Scopes**: `afw_xctx_scope_t` — pool `p`, `block`, `parent_lexical_scope`, RC, `frame_slots[]` indexed by `afw_value_block_symbol_t.index`. Activate on stack; resolve by lexical depth + index. Assignment stores into `frame_slots[]` (may wrap escaping lambdas in `closure_binding`).

## Memory (short)
Hierarchical pools (incl. xctx/scope). Bulk free on pool/scope release; **RC only for escaping values** (e.g. closures keep a reference to a scope). Long-running polish: managed `optional_release` / clone-or-reference on escaping objects/lists/closures/`compiled_value`, and allocate evaluation results in current `scope->p` — see `afw-value-memory`.

## Eval / control flow
`afw_xctx_t`: scope stack, evaluation stack, **qualifier stack**, **`statement_flow`** (sequential / break / continue / return / rethrow) — script leave paths are flags, not C exceptions. Built-ins and script functions unify via call nodes; polymorphic built-ins resolve from first arg type at runtime.

**Qualifier stack:** hot path is `qualifier::name` (`get_cb`, most recent matching visible entry). List/debug snapshots are `qualifier()` / `qualifiers()` via `contribute_cb` (multi-entry, can be large) — see **`afw-qualified-variables`** (issue **#9**).

## Design philosophy
Immutability first; pool-centric lifetimes; metadata as single source of truth; curated TypeScript-like surface (lambdas, destructuring, types — not prototypes/loose JS). Prefer small patterned pieces over one-off machinery.

## Naming values (short)
- Structured values: **object** (named **properties**) and **array** (ordered). Do not call objects “bags” — **bag** is historical (XACML → list → array); see always-on `afw-project` terminology.
- Object **meta** is sideband, separate from the property map.

## Process glue
Capabilities (functions, data types, adapters, content types, …) are **registered into the environment** — core at create (`afw_environment_register_core.c` after `afw_generated_register`), extensions/commands later via the same APIs. See `afw-environment`.

**Compile → value → evaluate:** `afw-compile` / `afw-compiler-ebnf` → graph in `value/` → `afw-script-eval`; built-ins in `afw-function`. Expression compile needs `prepare_environment` after functions are registered.

## Use cases that drive design
Authorization policies, object mapping, compile-once long-running subscribers (global/parent pool), NL→script tools, embedded.

## Where in the tree
`src/afw` module map / headers / adapter-env services: `afw-core-layout`, `afw-headers`, `afw-core-services`, `afw-environment`.
